==A Legend On the Loose==
With [[Celio]]'s Network Machine fully upgraded, there have been recent sightings of a mysterious, quick-footed Pokémon. This Pokémon has found its way here from the neighboring [[Johto]] region and begins [[Roaming Pokémon|roaming]] across [[Kanto]]. The creature that appears will have a type advantage against your [[first partner Pokémon]].

'''Before trying to track it down, be sure to save your progress'''. Due to {{DL|List of battle glitches in Generation III|Roaming Roar bug|a glitch}}, {{p|Entei}} and {{p|Raikou}} will permanently disappear if they are able to use {{m|Roar}} to escape. If you have not yet used the [[Master Ball]], doing so when the battle begins is the easiest way to avoid this scenario; players may also use a [[soft reset]] to reload the game from the last save. Otherwise, players would need to play through a new game to make the beast reappear. Thankfully, this bug was fixed in the [[Nintendo Switch]] re-release of the games.

===Tracking a Beast===
The Pokémon now races across the vast [[Kanto]] region, but it is not necessary to search every area for it. A simple strategy involves spraying on a Repel.

