===Rival Battle 9===
{{ga|Blue}} has swapped out his {{p|Pidgeot}} and {{p|Rhydon}} for {{p|Heracross}} and {{p|Tyranitar}}. Most of his Pokémon also have moves to cover their weaknesses. Heracross takes massive damage from {{t|Flying}} attacks, but avoid using Flying-type Pokémon as it can fight back with {{m|Rock Tomb}}. Similarly, Tyranitar suffers massive damage from {{t|Fighting}} moves, but Fighting-type Pokémon will be vulnerable to {{m|Aerial Ace}}, a Flying-type attack. His {{p|Arcanine}}, {{p|Gyarados}}, and {{p|Exeggutor}} are much the same as before. Arcanine can counter {{t|Rock}} Pokémon with {{m|Iron Tail}}, and Gyarados can retaliate against {{t|Electric}} Pokémon with {{m|Earthquake}}. {{p|Charizard}}, {{p|Blastoise}}, and {{p|Venusaur}} all have ways to counter their weaknesses, so be wary of sending in a Pokémon that may seemingly have the advantage at first.

